SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] running — 3 × 800 m at 5:10–5:20/km with 90 sec 
 standing recovery\, tot
DESCRIPTION:3 × 800 m at 5:10–5:20/km with 90 sec standing recovery\, to
 tal ~30 min including warm-up and cool-down\; cut session short if HR exce
 eds 160 bpm.\n\nReason: With only one run in 4 weeks (at 169 bpm average) 
 and the 10K just 4 days away\, a full 6-rep interval session risks excessi
 ve neuromuscular fatigue at exactly the wrong moment — a reduced stimulu
 s maintains sharpness without digging a hole.\n\nAI coaching 2026-10-03
END:VEVENT
