SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] running — Cap at 13–14 km at 6:30–7:00/km (appr
 oximately 90–100 min) —
DESCRIPTION:Cap at 13–14 km at 6:30–7:00/km (approximately 90–100 min
 ) — do not attempt the full 17.6 km this soon after back-to-back race we
 eks with low sleep and minimal run base.\n\nReason: With only one run in t
 he last 4 weeks and two races in consecutive weekends\, jumping straight t
 o a 17.6 km long run carries significant injury risk — a shorter aerobic
  run rebuilds the base safely and still supports the marathon block ahead.
 \n\nAI coaching 2026-10-03
